{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":".claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":651,"code_snippet":"yq -o=json -I0 '.' \"$ledger\" 2>/dev/null | jq -e --arg src ... >/dev/null 2>&1","reasoning_trace":"Read _fr11_spike_decided; no pipefail, function status is jq's; jq 1.6 -e exits 0 on empty input. Reproduced: unparsable ledger + git branch -D spike/x -> hook exit 0. PR test spike-validator 16 fails.","finding":"FR-1.1 decided-spike unlock fails open on an unparsable ledger","critique":"Header promises any failed lookup keeps the block; code allows the delete on the most common jq.","remediation":"Capture yq output, require non-empty valid JSON before jq -e; or set -o pipefail and test pipeline status.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-754 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-002","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":".claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":691,"code_snippet":"if [[ \"$name\" == spike/* ]] && _fr11_spike_decided \"${name#spike/}\"; then continue; fi","reasoning_trace":"Unlock checks ledger row only; hooks-reference row requires refs/remotes/origin/spike/<slug> with local as ancestor. Reproduced: origin lacks spike/x, decided operator row -> git branch -D spike/x allowed.","finding":"Decided-spike unlock never verifies the spike was pushed","critique":"The accepted forged-row risk assumed the branch is already pushed; without the check a forged row deletes the only copy.","remediation":"Require git rev-parse refs/remotes/origin/spike/<slug> and merge-base --is-ancestor; add negative test.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-284 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/284.html","CWE-1068 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-003","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":".claude/hooks/safety/block-destructive-bash.sh","line":867,"code_snippet":"if [[ \"$command\" == *\"spike/\"* ]]; then ... (merge|rebase|pull|cherry-pick) ... checkout ... restore ... gh pr create","reasoning_trace":"Probed head hook: git push origin spike/x:main, push HEAD:main on spike, branch -f/-m/-c, update-ref, reset --soft, read-tree, checkout -p, fetch && merge FETCH_HEAD, gh api pulls, config alias all exit 0. hooks-reference SP-1 row lists these as covered.","finding":"SP-1 misses the direct routes that land spike content on another branch","critique":"The rule implements about half of its documented coverage and its misses comment omits checkout -p and read-tree.","remediation":"Extend SP-1 to push refspecs, branch -f/-m/-M/-c/-C, update-ref, reset, read-tree, checkout -p, same-line FETCH_HEAD merge, gh api pulls, alias definitions; add corpus rows.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-693 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html","CWE-1068 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-004","category":"security","criterion":"authorization","severity":"HIGH","score":3,"file":".claude/scripts/chart-guard.sh","line":42,"code_snippet":"ctx=\"$(\"$DW\" context --prd \"${ROOT}/grimoires/loa/prd.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -n 1)\" || ctx=\"unknown\"","reasoning_trace":"dec-write-lib.sh op_context prints the verdict from live signals only and lists the PRD signal as advisory under --why. Reproduced: autonomous PRD Status -> guard prints interactive, exit 0; CD-10 fails; chart.md:79-82 and guard header claim a refusal.","finding":"Interactive-only guard does not refuse the autonomous-PRD context it documents","critique":"Three artifacts (header, command doc, test) promise a control the code does not implement.","remediation":"Read context --why --prd and treat a prd signal as unattended in the guard and op_close, or remove the clause from header, chart.md and CD-10.","confidence":"medium","references":["CWE-1068 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1068.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-005","category":"security","criterion":"input_validation","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":".claude/scripts/chart-ticket.sh","line":458,"code_snippet":"bad=\"$(comm -13 <(LC_ALL=C sort -u \"$m\") <(printf '%s\\n' \"$after\" | LC_ALL=C sort -u) | awk ... p !~ /^grimoires\\/loa\\/research\\// ...)\"","reasoning_trace":"Status-line set compare: overwrites of pre-dirty tracked, pre-existing untracked or ignored files add no line. Marker lives under research/, the whitelisted directory the subagent may Write. .git/ never appears in status. Reproduced overwrite -> research-end exit 0. Dissent DISS-001/DISS-C-001 confirm.","finding":"Research scope check blind to overwrites, forgeable by the subagent, never sees .git/","critique":"The only mechanical fence on a write-capable subagent that ingests arbitrary web pages is defeatable three ways.","remediation":"Fingerprint content (git write-tree + sha256 of untracked/ignored), store the marker outside research/, snapshot .git/hooks, .git/config, for-each-ref.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-345 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/345.html","OWASP LLM01 https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm01-prompt-injection/"]}
{"id":"SEC-006","category":"security","criterion":"confidentiality_integrity","severity":"HIGH","score":2,"file":".claude/scripts/chart-unblock-probe.sh","line":66,"code_snippet":"(cd \"$WT\" && run_with_timeout \"$TIMEOUT\" \"$@\")","reasoning_trace":"Skill has deny_raw_shell and allowlists this helper with args *, so it is the only arbitrary-command path. Reproduced: probe prints MY_API_KEY, creates branch/tag/config in the main repo (shared .git), helper exits 0. scripts-reference says scrubbed environment.","finding":"Probe helper inherits the full environment, shares .git, and reports unchanged on ref/config/hook writes","critique":"The documented containment boundary scrubs nothing and watches only git status text.","remediation":"env -i with an allowlist; snapshot for-each-ref, .git/config, .git/hooks; compare content hashes; consider a clone instead of a linked worktree.","confidence":"high","references":["CWE-668 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/668.html","CWE-250 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/250.html","OWASP LLM02 https://genai.owasp.org/llmrisk/llm022025-sensitive-information-disclosure/"]}
